  "kind": "quirk",
  "title": "ISOWEEKNUM truncates the serial and returns week 52 for serial 0 (1900-01-00) and 1 (1900-01-01)",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0 build 20430, ISOWEEKNUM(date) truncates date to a whole serial in [0, 2958465] without half-second time rounding and computes the Monday-based ISO week containing the serial's Thursday. On Excel's fictitious 1900-01-00 (serial 0, Saturday) and 1900-01-01 (serial 1, Sunday), the ISO year is 1899 and ISOWEEKNUM returns 52. All 10,153 full-bank ISOWEEKNUM rows match.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured in CalcFunc-Evidence runs/w111-broad-20260929/answers/answers-isoweeknum.json.gz (Excel 16.0 build 20430) and matched on 10,153/10,153 full-bank rows.",
